       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen at 9,600 mg/day is about 3 times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication for it. At that dose the risk of serious harm is high. That includes GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis, and it applies even to a patient with normal kidney and liver function. I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you have a reason for this dose that I don't know about, you can contact pharmacy directly to discuss it. They can review it and handle it through the proper override process. I'm happy to help with a different order, or with a note to pharmacy about the dosing question."
